WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:32.701
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:32.971 --> 00:34.014
[This drama is fiction.]

3
00:34.014 --> 00:36.141
[Characters, places, events, organization, and the setting have no connection to reality.]

4
00:36.141 --> 00:38.543
[Child actors were filmed under safe conditions.]

5
00:41.897 --> 00:43.814
Counsel for the defendant?

6
00:43.814 --> 00:47.464
Why don't we settle this and wrap it up here?

7
00:49.897 --> 00:51.581
We cannot settle.

8
00:51.581 --> 00:55.691
Your Honor, not all affairs are the same.

9
00:55.691 --> 00:58.237
An affair is an affair.

10
00:58.237 --> 01:02.047
Are you claiming there are degrees of illegality in an affair?

11
01:02.772 --> 01:04.172
No.

12
01:05.117 --> 01:08.392
I'm claiming there is no illegality.

13
01:21.773 --> 01:27.953
[Case 01: Good Partner]

14
01:28.981 --> 01:33.098
We will now begin the presentation of the Power Woman of the Year award.

15
01:33.098 --> 01:37.423
The winner is Attorney Cha Eun Kyung.

16
01:40.897 --> 01:47.045
She built a law firm with 50 people in just three years.

17
01:47.045 --> 01:50.230
Congratulations on your award.

18
01:50.230 --> 01:54.605
A lawyer who puts skill, principles, and people first.

19
01:54.605 --> 01:59.349
Selected as one of today's most notable female leaders,

20
01:59.349 --> 02:05.022
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung. Please give her a warm round of applause.

21
02:11.147 --> 02:14.480
Attorney Cha, please introduce yourself.

22
02:14.480 --> 02:18.658
Hello. I'm the representative attorney of Korea's only divorce law firm,

23
02:18.658 --> 02:21.824
Cha Eun Kyung from REBOM Law Firm.

24
02:21.824 --> 02:23.849
Nice to meet you.

25
02:27.439 --> 02:31.981
REBOM has seen remarkable growth in just three years.

26
02:31.981 --> 02:36.339
What is the secret to such rapid growth?

27
02:37.742 --> 02:39.416
Sales skills.

28
02:39.416 --> 02:41.397
Sales... skills?

29
02:41.397 --> 02:44.689
Do you mean marketing or promotion?

30
02:44.689 --> 02:45.980
No.

31
02:45.980 --> 02:50.265
Sales skills ultimately come from sincerity.

32
02:50.265 --> 02:55.489
There are 36,000 lawyers now, and 27,000 of them are in Seoul.

33
02:55.489 --> 03:00.160
The only way to survive this jungle is not to take on cases,

34
03:00.160 --> 03:02.999
but to provide solutions for the clients' lives.

35
03:02.999 --> 03:06.987
The best result is the best sales pitch.

36
03:06.987 --> 03:13.264
"The best result is the best sales pitch." That's a great quote.

37
03:13.264 --> 03:15.759
Now I can't help but wonder.

38
03:15.759 --> 03:18.345
What is REBOM's next goal?

39
03:18.345 --> 03:21.230
REBOM is preparing for an expansion.

40
03:21.230 --> 03:27.355
We plan to reach 30 billion won in sales and enter the top 30 firms in Korea.

41
03:27.355 --> 03:29.908
We'll be rooting for you.

42
03:38.172 --> 03:43.339
That was this year's Power Woman, Attorney Cha Eun Kyung.

43
03:59.004 --> 04:01.047
[Central Family Court]

44
04:27.475 --> 04:30.422
[REBOM Law Firm]

45
04:37.750 --> 04:40.479
Good morning, ma'am.

46
04:44.090 --> 04:45.786
Hello.

47
04:47.104 --> 04:50.606
- Good morning. - Hello.

48
04:51.482 --> 04:53.897
- Hello. - Good morning.

49
04:53.897 --> 04:55.996
The Senior Partner is here.

50
04:56.598 --> 04:58.940
Selected as Korea's Power Woman.

51
04:58.940 --> 05:00.891
Congratulations.

52
05:04.856 --> 05:08.371
Ma'am, how about a team dinner tonight?

53
05:08.371 --> 05:09.411
A team dinner.

54
05:09.411 --> 05:14.833
- Team dinner. - Team dinner.

55
05:14.833 --> 05:18.187
Wait a minute.

56
05:18.187 --> 05:21.892
Let's have it when we expand to the eighth floor.

57
05:23.272 --> 05:25.680
Yes. Shall we? That would be better.

58
05:25.680 --> 05:29.522
To be exact, I'm the one who won the award, not REBOM, right?

59
05:29.522 --> 05:33.047
Let's break it up and get back to work. Thank you.

60
05:36.397 --> 05:41.512
She's saying we should share the joy when it's not a personal event

61
05:41.512 --> 05:44.532
but a celebration for all of us.

62
05:44.532 --> 05:47.744
Yes. Please get back to what you need to do.

63
05:48.522 --> 05:51.214
I told you not to use confetti. Thank you.

64
06:01.194 --> 06:02.594
What?

65
06:05.647 --> 06:08.814
Congratulations again, ma'am.

66
06:08.814 --> 06:11.214
I'll put this over there.

67
06:11.981 --> 06:14.531
I told them you don't like parties,

68
06:14.531 --> 06:17.390
but they all insisted on celebrating.

69
06:19.192 --> 06:24.273
Ma'am, we're in Season 2 now. Will we be okay like this?

70
06:24.273 --> 06:25.314
Season 2?

71
06:25.314 --> 06:29.981
We're not a small office anymore. We're a firm with 50 employees.

72
06:29.981 --> 06:32.649
So it's Season 2 of REBOM.

73
06:32.649 --> 06:34.355
But it's an emergency, ma'am.

74
06:34.355 --> 06:41.089
A big firm like this only has two lawyers: you and me.

75
06:41.910 --> 06:44.251
I let them go because they deserved it.

76
06:44.251 --> 06:48.772
They don't care about cases and only talk about shares. What kind of lawyers are they?

77
06:48.772 --> 06:52.434
Make me a partner. We need to share profits for the firm to grow.

78
06:52.434 --> 06:54.106
Should've handled your cases first.

79
06:54.106 --> 06:56.771
Why talk about shares when you lack basics?

80
06:56.771 --> 06:59.698
You hand our cases to other firms and take referral fees.

81
06:59.698 --> 07:02.939
Are you a lawyer or a broker? That's illegal.

82
07:02.939 --> 07:04.738
So what? Are you going to sue me?

83
07:04.738 --> 07:08.950
Don't come in tomorrow. You did nothing, so there's nothing to pass on.

84
07:08.950 --> 07:10.362
[Kim Hyun Min] [Heo Jin Kyung]

85
07:14.522 --> 07:17.834
I don't need people who care about their own interests and shares,

86
07:17.834 --> 07:22.026
not the clients' interests, at a firm I built with my own blood and sweat.

87
07:22.697 --> 07:26.224
I'll train a good associate and make them a partner.

88
07:26.224 --> 07:28.990
That's when Season 2 of REBOM really begins.

89
07:28.990 --> 07:30.388
You said you wouldn't do it.

90
07:30.388 --> 07:33.224
It's not that I won't. It's that I can't.

91
07:33.224 --> 07:37.272
I'm the type who needs time to myself after work, not more sales work...

92
07:37.272 --> 07:38.998
Anyway, that's not the point.

93
07:38.998 --> 07:41.107
Ma'am, please make sure

94
07:41.107 --> 07:45.647
to hire a lawyer who will stay with us for a long time, and do it quickly.

95
07:45.647 --> 07:48.054
- I'm counting on you. - I got it. Back to work.

96
07:48.054 --> 07:49.454
Got it.

97
08:02.472 --> 08:06.588
Good lawyers are so hard to find.

98
08:14.430 --> 08:16.472
[REBOM Law Firm eighth floor expansion plan]

99
08:25.355 --> 08:26.689
Ma'am.

100
08:26.689 --> 08:31.261
Another firm took our ad spot by paying double the deposit.

101
08:31.261 --> 08:32.805
What?

102
08:32.805 --> 08:36.205
We were going to use that spot to promote the eighth floor.

103
08:38.325 --> 08:40.159
[Skill is the strategy]

104
09:29.046 --> 09:31.573
[Problem Solver Kang Hye Seong]

105
09:46.288 --> 09:48.909
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm's Problem Solver] [Attorney Kang Hye Seong]

106
10:02.278 --> 10:06.292
[For Divorce Cases, Kang Hye Seong]

107
10:13.355 --> 10:15.897
Please wait over there, thank you.

108
10:15.897 --> 10:17.480
Hello.

109
10:17.480 --> 10:19.814
Village Chief.

110
10:19.814 --> 10:22.602
Isn't Attorney Kang Hye Seong here yet?

111
10:22.602 --> 10:25.083
She went to court, but she'll be back soon.

112
10:25.083 --> 10:26.380
Oh, there she is.

113
10:26.380 --> 10:27.731
Attorney Kang.

114
10:27.731 --> 10:30.919
Village Chief. You shouldn't bring so much food every time.

115
10:30.919 --> 10:33.446
We won the case because of you.

116
10:33.446 --> 10:38.744
How did you turn around a case we completely lost in the first trial?

117
10:39.636 --> 10:41.439
[Court]

118
10:41.439 --> 10:43.414
The defendant's dog barks every night

119
10:43.414 --> 10:45.495
causing the plaintiff chronic headaches,

120
10:45.495 --> 10:47.643
so the claim for damages was granted.

121
10:47.643 --> 10:49.586
Since defendant lost the first trial,

122
10:49.586 --> 10:52.462
it's hard to hold further hearings without new evidence.

123
10:52.462 --> 10:55.814
I take it you have no new evidence to present?

124
10:55.814 --> 10:58.505
Your Honor, I have evidence.

125
11:01.147 --> 11:03.226
Do you know this dog?

126
11:03.226 --> 11:05.520
- I know Bokdong. - Does he bark a lot?

127
11:05.520 --> 11:07.493
- He doesn't. - Bokdong's a good boy.

128
11:07.493 --> 11:09.230
- A good boy? - Yes.

129
11:09.230 --> 11:13.647
Ma'am, could I take a look at the security camera footage?

130
11:13.647 --> 11:14.779
Can I help you?

131
11:14.779 --> 11:16.623
Could I check the dashcam footage?

132
11:16.623 --> 11:21.689
Based on the neighbors' statements and the security camera investigation,

133
11:21.689 --> 11:25.172
the defendant's dog didn't bark for no reason.

134
11:26.064 --> 11:31.588
He barked instinctively whenever someone tried to break into the plaintiff's house.

135
11:31.588 --> 11:37.363
Thanks to the defendant's dog, the plaintiff was able to prevent a break-in.

136
11:38.147 --> 11:41.438
A dog's instinctive reaction to a dangerous situation

137
11:41.438 --> 11:45.134
can't be called illegal noise beyond what neighbors should bear.

138
11:45.134 --> 11:47.273
Thank you so much, Attorney Kang.

139
11:47.273 --> 11:50.064
For letting me live with Bokdong again.

140
11:50.064 --> 11:53.158
I'm so grateful that I would like to refer a case to you.

141
11:53.158 --> 11:55.981
Do you handle divorce cases too?

142
11:55.981 --> 11:59.714
Yes, of course! Divorce cases are my absolute favorite.

143
12:01.517 --> 12:03.278
That's good.

144
12:05.897 --> 12:07.393
Yes.

145
12:08.959 --> 12:13.314
Attorney Kang, are you working late again?

146
12:13.314 --> 12:18.112
You're the only lawyer here, yet you take on every minor case that comes in.

147
12:18.112 --> 12:20.612
It's not like this firm specializes in them.

148
12:20.612 --> 12:25.423
How can you handle all these people and all these different fields alone?

149
12:26.860 --> 12:28.718
Escape while you can.

150
12:30.519 --> 12:35.105
But thanks to the boss, these minor... I mean,

151
12:35.105 --> 12:38.731
I'm getting experience with various cases.

152
12:38.731 --> 12:40.073
Well,

153
12:40.073 --> 12:43.045
at least you have a divorce consultation tomorrow, and you like those.

154
12:45.540 --> 12:49.076
[CHUNJEONG Law Firm]

155
12:56.397 --> 12:58.592
What is the reason for the divorce?

156
12:59.439 --> 13:03.178
My wife... had an affair.

157
13:15.274 --> 13:17.420
The evidence is sufficient.

158
13:17.420 --> 13:19.188
You'll proceed with the divorce, right?

159
13:19.188 --> 13:21.214
I'm such a fool.

160
13:22.647 --> 13:27.880
My feelings don't just disappear even if she cheated.

161
13:29.498 --> 13:31.606
I loved her so much...

162
13:33.790 --> 13:35.287
But still,

163
13:36.272 --> 13:40.172
it was a very difficult decision for me to get a divorce.

164
13:42.522 --> 13:44.397
That's wise.

165
13:44.397 --> 13:48.839
I often see people who just forgive and move on after going through this.

166
13:49.969 --> 13:52.561
If she did wrong, you should get a divorce.

167
13:56.814 --> 14:00.031
Based on this evidence, you have a 99% chance of winning.

168
14:00.031 --> 14:01.725
It's clearly an affair.

169
14:12.013 --> 14:13.920
[Motel Shim]

170
14:13.920 --> 14:19.089
Is it a 100% chance I'll get divorced?

171
14:19.089 --> 14:24.623
Not 100%, but about 99%.

172
14:25.731 --> 14:28.630
Then there's no hope...

173
14:29.605 --> 14:31.742
Even if it's a 99% losing case,

174
14:31.742 --> 14:36.071
it's our job to fight for that 1% chance.

175
14:36.071 --> 14:37.815
Judges are human too.

176
14:37.815 --> 14:41.138
We can't predict a verdict with 100% certainty.

177
14:41.138 --> 14:47.361
Once you receive the complaint, I'll look for even a 1% opening to rebut it.

178
14:47.361 --> 14:51.135
I really don't want to get divorced.

179
14:51.135 --> 14:53.623
This is my second marriage.

180
14:53.623 --> 14:55.864
I can't get divorced twice.

181
14:55.864 --> 14:59.438
That's why I came to REBOM Law Firm, the best in the industry.

182
14:59.438 --> 15:02.179
Please help me.

183
15:02.179 --> 15:07.897
Since your husband wants a divorce, he'll be sending a complaint soon.

184
15:07.897 --> 15:11.131
Come back then, and we'll have another consultation.

185
15:13.023 --> 15:15.137
What does your asset situation look like?

186
15:15.137 --> 15:16.817
Don't even get me started.

187
15:16.817 --> 15:20.188
My father gave my wife a condo worth 100 million won.

188
15:20.188 --> 15:23.856
I was going to sell it and expand the stray dog shelter.

189
15:23.856 --> 15:25.740
I really want that money back.

190
15:25.740 --> 15:30.449
It's getting hotter, and my dogs need to be in a better facility.

191
15:30.449 --> 15:33.183
So please end the lawsuit quickly.

192
15:34.397 --> 15:38.768
Sadly, I can't promise a quick divorce with no property division for her.

193
15:38.768 --> 15:42.929
A lawyer can't customize a ruling like that.

194
15:43.682 --> 15:45.910
For property division...

195
15:45.910 --> 15:48.480
it'll be at least 30 million won.

196
15:48.480 --> 15:50.221
What?

197
15:50.221 --> 15:55.123
You want me to give 30 million won to a woman who cheated?

198
15:55.123 --> 15:56.838
I know it sounds unfair.

199
15:56.838 --> 16:02.397
What I don't get is why the law gives property division to the one who cheated.

200
16:02.397 --> 16:05.435
But we'll offset the division with the compensation she owes.

201
16:05.435 --> 16:07.823
And try our best to get the condo back.

202
16:07.823 --> 16:09.472
Okay.

203
16:10.689 --> 16:15.522
I'm counting on you. Please make sure I get this divorce.

204
16:15.522 --> 16:16.665
She's too clingy.

205
16:16.665 --> 16:19.477
With someone like that, a quick divorce is the answer.

206
16:19.477 --> 16:21.272
I'll file the complaint now.

207
16:21.272 --> 16:22.672
Yes.

208
16:24.839 --> 16:26.058
Mom.

209
16:26.058 --> 16:27.317
Hey.

210
16:29.238 --> 16:30.651
Good job today.

211
16:30.651 --> 16:32.040
Aren't you tired?

212
16:32.040 --> 16:33.637
I'm okay.

213
16:45.360 --> 16:48.976
You promised to rest on the days you go to your dad's.

214
16:48.976 --> 16:50.698
Stop looking at the workbook.

215
16:50.698 --> 16:54.411
No, it's inefficient to space out in the car.

216
16:55.202 --> 16:58.516
You know, since high school, you're becoming less and less human.

217
16:58.516 --> 16:59.978
Guess who I take after.

218
16:59.978 --> 17:03.355
Mom, I'm switching to Ji Yoon's math academy.

219
17:03.355 --> 17:06.397
Why? Don't you like the one you go to now?

220
17:06.397 --> 17:08.188
I'll look for a new place for you.

221
17:08.188 --> 17:11.183
How many times have you said that? I'll handle it myself.

222
17:11.183 --> 17:14.587
Civil Code Article 4: A person reaches adulthood at the age of 19.

223
17:14.587 --> 17:16.819
I'll be an adult in three years.

224
17:33.735 --> 17:35.401
Welcome, Jae Hee.

225
17:40.867 --> 17:42.267
Jae Hee.

226
17:43.064 --> 17:44.850
- I'll go in first. - Okay.

227
17:44.850 --> 17:46.724
Drive safely, Mom.

228
17:47.772 --> 17:50.910
These are frozen dumplings. Jae Hee really likes them.

229
17:50.910 --> 17:52.646
Keep them home for her.

230
17:55.797 --> 17:57.489
Could you do that, please?

231
17:58.766 --> 18:00.639
Jae Hee eats dumplings?

232
18:00.639 --> 18:02.188
She used to not like them.

233
18:02.188 --> 18:05.725
She didn't like store-bought ones. She liked homemade ones.

234
18:05.725 --> 18:08.198
You made dumplings yourself?

235
18:08.198 --> 18:11.855
No, when would I have time for that? Ji Yoon's mom did.

236
18:11.855 --> 18:13.955
Ta-da!

237
18:13.955 --> 18:16.201
- Thank you. - Eat up.

238
18:18.411 --> 18:21.754
Jae Hee wants to switch math academies.

239
18:21.754 --> 18:23.151
I'll change it and let you know.

240
18:23.151 --> 18:25.386
Thanks. Go on.

241
18:25.386 --> 18:26.731
Yeah.

242
18:26.731 --> 18:29.397
- I'll win for sure. - I'll definitely win.

243
18:29.397 --> 18:32.355
Jae Hee, want Dad to roast one? I'm a marshmallow expert.

244
18:32.355 --> 18:35.105
You always burn them, Dad.

245
18:35.105 --> 18:36.731
Honey, I'll do it.

246
18:36.731 --> 18:40.397
- I'm good at this. - Just wait.

247
18:40.397 --> 18:42.856
- I won. - No, you didn't.

248
18:42.856 --> 18:44.563
- I'm really good at this. - No.

249
18:44.563 --> 18:46.920
Let's see.

250
18:55.301 --> 18:56.932
[Manage My Cases]

251
18:56.932 --> 18:57.982
[Ongoing Case]

252
19:00.435 --> 19:02.188
[Search]

253
19:04.032 --> 19:05.434
[Counsel for Defendant]

254
19:07.210 --> 19:09.210
[REBOM Attorneys: Cha Eun Kyung, Jeon Eun Ho]

255
19:29.929 --> 19:32.661
Wow, it's the Han River.

256
19:43.772 --> 19:46.833
I'll only attend the first hearing for today's trial.

257
19:46.833 --> 19:50.385
Per contract, you will handle it from the second hearing.

258
19:50.385 --> 19:51.863
Yes, ma'am.

259
19:51.863 --> 19:53.856
- Ma'am. - Yes?

260
19:53.856 --> 19:56.461
Actually, I'm a bit worried lately.

261
19:56.461 --> 20:00.062
What senior partner goes to court this often?

262
20:00.062 --> 20:02.897
Between trials, sales, consultations, and TV work...

263
20:02.897 --> 20:07.598
I'm so anxious that you might get burned out.

264
20:07.598 --> 20:09.009
So if you ask me,

265
20:09.009 --> 20:13.480
it would be great to hire a new lawyer soon. What do you think?

266
20:13.480 --> 20:15.647
You're worried about me, right?

267
20:15.647 --> 20:16.981
Of course. Definitely.

268
20:16.981 --> 20:21.724
And actually, I'm a bit worried about myself. I need my own time after work.

269
20:21.724 --> 20:26.500
But since I don't have that lately, I wonder if this is what they call overwork.

270
20:26.500 --> 20:29.439
What do you think about that?

271
20:29.439 --> 20:34.463
Attorney Jeon, do you smile like that while attacking your opponent in court?

272
20:34.463 --> 20:36.048
You're good at this.

273
20:36.048 --> 20:37.689
Thank you.

274
20:37.689 --> 20:40.322
We're in the middle of hiring, so don't worry.

275
20:40.322 --> 20:41.640
Yes, ma'am.

276
21:05.230 --> 21:06.522
Seo Ji Hoon?

277
21:06.522 --> 21:08.297
Yes, Attorney.

278
21:10.052 --> 21:12.814
Was the traffic heavy?

279
21:12.814 --> 21:14.731
The trial is still five minutes away.

280
21:14.731 --> 21:18.397
Yes, but I'm a bit nervous.

281
21:18.397 --> 21:21.509
The other side is the famous Cha Eun Kyung's firm.

282
21:21.509 --> 21:23.188
Will we be okay?

283
21:23.188 --> 21:25.557
The head of the firm rarely appears in person.

284
21:25.557 --> 21:28.522
And why be anxious? Their fault is clear.

285
21:28.522 --> 21:31.814
You'll be relieved once you see how I present the case.

286
21:31.814 --> 21:33.308
Let's go in.

287
21:45.772 --> 21:47.553
It's Cha Eun Kyung.

288
22:05.860 --> 22:07.510
Let's go too.

289
22:10.439 --> 22:14.064
Attorney Kang Hye Seong of CHUNJEONG Law Firm is present.

290
22:14.064 --> 22:17.630
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung of REBOM Law Firm is present.

291
22:23.439 --> 22:27.032
Your Honor, he's the one who cheated first.

292
22:27.032 --> 22:29.696
He's doing this to pin everything on me.

293
22:35.731 --> 22:37.793
What are you talking about?

294
22:37.793 --> 22:40.470
The defendant cheated, not the plaintiff.

295
22:40.470 --> 22:43.220
Your Honor, please show the evidence.

296
22:45.434 --> 22:48.136
[Is there anyone who can meet around 9:00 PM tonight?]

297
22:48.136 --> 22:49.604
[Let's meet at Hotel Argen in Seoul]

298
22:49.604 --> 22:51.142
[Whoever gets there first, message me]

299
23:08.856 --> 23:13.081
I won't agree to a divorce. Please protect my family, Your Honor.

300
23:13.081 --> 23:16.606
I really, really didn't sleep with anyone.

301
23:17.981 --> 23:19.526
You went to the motel...

302
23:21.121 --> 23:24.355
You went to the motel, but you didn't sleep with anyone?

303
23:24.355 --> 23:27.147
Hey, you know I really didn't sleep with anyone!

304
23:27.147 --> 23:28.886
Order in the court.

305
23:30.814 --> 23:36.000
You say there was no sex, despite all this evidence of seeking partners?

306
23:36.000 --> 23:38.428
This is a court of law.

307
23:39.282 --> 23:41.825
The plaintiff's counsel traveled a long way,

308
23:41.825 --> 23:44.860
so she may have missed our evidence from this morning.

309
23:44.860 --> 23:46.675
Could you please display it?

310
24:06.766 --> 24:08.856
They both cheated?

311
24:14.064 --> 24:17.564
The plaintiff was the one who cheated first.

312
24:17.564 --> 24:22.516
And the defendant's affair was due to the plaintiff's threats and coercion.

313
24:22.516 --> 24:24.698
Threats and coercion?

314
24:24.698 --> 24:29.134
Who in their right mind would threaten their spouse into having an affair?

315
24:29.134 --> 24:31.250
He's sitting right next to you.

316
24:31.250 --> 24:33.529
I guess you didn't know, Counselor.

317
24:37.439 --> 24:40.210
Your false claims are excessive. Can you prove them?

318
24:40.210 --> 24:43.111
Yes. Digital forensics is currently underway.

319
24:44.272 --> 24:45.380
Your Honor.

320
24:45.380 --> 24:47.792
Please record that the defendant's counsel

321
24:47.792 --> 24:50.814
just admitted to the defendant's infidelity.

322
24:50.814 --> 24:54.590
Go ahead. We admit to the "act" of infidelity.

323
24:54.590 --> 24:57.647
She's admitting it? In court?

324
24:57.647 --> 24:59.468
We admit the act itself.

325
24:59.468 --> 25:03.731
However, that act does not make her the party at fault.

326
25:03.731 --> 25:07.755
If you're so desperate to get it on the record, by all means.

327
25:22.085 --> 25:23.635
Seo Ji Hoon.

328
25:27.132 --> 25:30.922
Seo Ji Hoon, you should have told me that you also had an affair.

329
25:31.857 --> 25:33.821
I'm sorry.

330
25:33.821 --> 25:37.647
I only suggested we both admit it and divorce by mutual agreement.

331
25:37.647 --> 25:42.940
But she refused to divorce me, so I had no choice but to file a lawsuit.

332
25:42.940 --> 25:45.298
I didn't know she had evidence.

333
25:46.188 --> 25:51.329
What about the claim that you threatened her to have sex with other men?

334
25:51.329 --> 25:53.561
That's absolutely not true. Never.

335
25:53.561 --> 25:56.159
Think about it. Why would I threaten her?

336
25:56.159 --> 25:59.988
She's lying to cover her own fault because she doesn't want a divorce.

337
25:59.988 --> 26:01.382
I see.

338
26:01.382 --> 26:03.054
Since both are at fault,

339
26:03.054 --> 26:06.373
I'll argue the marriage is broken to get a divorce ruling.

340
26:07.064 --> 26:09.272
You worked so hard today.

341
26:09.272 --> 26:11.272
- Great job. - Yes, we'll be in touch.

342
26:11.272 --> 26:14.029
- Yes, thank you. - Take care.

343
26:15.623 --> 26:17.023
- Thanks. - Good job.

344
26:17.023 --> 26:18.683
Secretary Kim is outside.

345
26:18.683 --> 26:20.406
Okay.

346
26:20.406 --> 26:21.972
Counselor!

347
26:23.997 --> 26:28.316
Counselor, so you're saying the plaintiff told the defendant to have an affair,

348
26:28.316 --> 26:31.658
and since she did as told, she's not at fault? Is that it?

349
26:31.658 --> 26:33.488
Exactly.

350
26:33.488 --> 26:35.246
If a client makes a ridiculous claim,

351
26:35.246 --> 26:38.401
isn't it a lawyer's job to refine it and present it to court?

352
26:38.401 --> 26:40.142
And when both sides are at fault,

353
26:40.142 --> 26:44.782
99% of lawyers propose a settlement instead of pushing an unreasonable claim.

354
26:44.782 --> 26:51.381
If that's all a lawyer does, an AI could do it. Why did you even show up?

355
26:52.125 --> 26:55.838
You said it's an absurd claim. By whose standards?

356
26:57.772 --> 27:00.969
This isn't your first divorce case, is it?

357
27:00.969 --> 27:02.643
Well, not exactly my first...

358
27:02.643 --> 27:07.641
Divorce cases are a 1% fight, not a 99% one.

359
27:07.641 --> 27:13.447
And there's no such thing as absurd in this world.

360
27:13.447 --> 27:15.476
That's normal for a rookie.

361
27:15.476 --> 27:18.701
Try to broaden your perspective.

362
27:22.497 --> 27:25.082
So, since we have different positions,

363
27:25.082 --> 27:29.105
I suppose she's saying we should both do our best for our clients.

364
27:29.105 --> 27:31.672
We'll see you at the next hearing, Counselor.

365
27:38.848 --> 27:42.168
Some lawyer she is.

366
27:46.861 --> 27:48.273
Please check here.

367
27:48.273 --> 27:50.230
Okay.

368
27:50.230 --> 27:52.850
- You're back, Attorney. - Yes.

369
27:55.113 --> 27:56.712
Just a moment.

370
27:58.689 --> 28:00.274
Yes.

371
28:04.439 --> 28:06.731
Attorney, how was it?

372
28:06.731 --> 28:09.196
It was a divorce trial in Seoul, which you love,

373
28:09.196 --> 28:13.601
and you even met a top-tier divorce lawyer.

374
28:13.601 --> 28:16.282
It was a mess on a whole other level.

375
28:16.282 --> 28:20.397
I thought he was the victim, but they both cheated.

376
28:20.397 --> 28:23.939
No way. He looked so innocent.

377
28:23.939 --> 28:25.489
Right?

378
28:25.489 --> 28:28.110
It was bad enough my client stabbed me in the back,

379
28:28.110 --> 28:32.480
but Attorney Cha Eun Kyung lied through her teeth rather than offer a settlement.

380
28:32.480 --> 28:34.634
I'm so disappointed.

381
28:34.634 --> 28:35.805
Seriously.

382
28:35.805 --> 28:38.486
Hey, Kang. Come to my office right now!

383
28:47.105 --> 28:50.271
Kang, wrap that case up quickly.

384
28:50.271 --> 28:53.147
A divorce rookie like you can never beat Cha Eun Kyung.

385
28:53.147 --> 28:57.499
Sir, I don't think fame and talent are proportional.

386
28:57.499 --> 29:00.565
I plan to do my best in this case too.

387
29:01.361 --> 29:04.184
Don't be stupid. It's a trial in Seoul.

388
29:04.184 --> 29:08.244
If it drags on, gas will cost more than the retainer fee.

389
29:08.244 --> 29:10.294
It's not cost-effective!

390
29:10.294 --> 29:11.769
Just settle.

391
29:12.919 --> 29:16.578
Sir, this is the first divorce case we have had in a year.

392
29:16.578 --> 29:19.272
Did you forget your promise when I joined the firm?

393
29:19.272 --> 29:22.813
[4 years ago] I want to become a divorce specialist.

394
29:22.813 --> 29:26.013
- Does CHUNJEONG get many divorce cases? - Of course.

395
29:26.013 --> 29:27.645
Tons of them.

396
29:28.622 --> 29:30.694
How long ago was that?

397
29:30.694 --> 29:32.434
Divorce doesn't make money.

398
29:32.434 --> 29:33.897
You may leave.

399
29:40.605 --> 29:42.005
Yes.

400
29:44.480 --> 29:47.352
Another stack coming in.

401
29:49.936 --> 29:52.727
[Jeon Eun Ho] You can't be serious.

402
29:52.727 --> 29:54.064
It must be tough.

403
29:54.064 --> 29:57.564
The two of you are handling over 100 cases right now.

404
29:57.564 --> 30:00.845
You should just become a partner and help her out, Attorney Jeon.

405
30:00.845 --> 30:04.950
You know better than anyone why she wants to grow the firm.

406
30:04.950 --> 30:06.367
- Manager Shim. - Yes?

407
30:06.367 --> 30:09.211
Do you know what I'm most confident in?

408
30:09.211 --> 30:10.705
Rocket divorces?

409
30:10.705 --> 30:12.605
You're great at finishing cases fast.

410
30:12.605 --> 30:14.314
Work-life balance?

411
30:14.314 --> 30:18.605
I heard you were a legend at a major law firm for always leaving right on time.

412
30:18.605 --> 30:20.965
Rocket divorces, work-life balance...

413
30:20.965 --> 30:22.489
It's not easy anymore.

414
30:22.489 --> 30:27.314
My specialty is metacognition. In other words, knowing my place.

415
30:27.314 --> 30:32.256
I'm just not partner material at all.

416
30:33.647 --> 30:36.772
Don't worry. We're in the middle of hiring.

417
30:36.772 --> 30:39.605
Anyway, enjoy your meal.

418
30:39.605 --> 30:41.856
Yes, enjoy your meal.

419
30:41.856 --> 30:44.415
- Ma'am, are you heading out to eat? - Yeah.

420
30:50.730 --> 30:52.652
If a client makes a ridiculous claim,

421
30:52.652 --> 30:56.188
isn't it a lawyer's job to refine it and present it to court?

422
30:56.188 --> 30:59.599
She's got guts for a rookie.

423
30:59.599 --> 31:00.880
Bingo.

424
31:00.880 --> 31:04.272
That was Attorney Kang Hye Seong, right? From earlier?

425
31:04.272 --> 31:06.605
No. Just eat.

426
31:06.605 --> 31:08.249
I thought she was cool.

427
31:08.249 --> 31:11.606
It was obvious her client stabbed her in the back,

428
31:11.606 --> 31:14.769
but she kept cool so the judge wouldn't notice.

429
31:15.919 --> 31:20.869
She was like, "Your false claims are excessive. Can you prove them?"

430
31:20.869 --> 31:23.232
- Are you serious? - Yes.

431
31:23.232 --> 31:26.036
I can't stand people with such narrow views.

432
31:29.154 --> 31:31.731
I have hired a new lawyer to start soon.

433
31:31.731 --> 31:34.897
Is a new lawyer finally coming?

434
31:34.897 --> 31:40.272
But did you find someone who meets your standards that quickly?

435
31:40.272 --> 31:42.349
- My standards? - Yes.

436
31:42.349 --> 31:45.105
At least five years' experience, serious about divorce,

437
31:45.105 --> 31:47.689
- Right. - and good at handling cases.

438
31:47.689 --> 31:52.376
Those three are actually quite strict standards.

439
31:52.376 --> 31:56.389
It's just that not many lawyers actually like divorce cases.

440
31:56.389 --> 32:01.582
And by their fifth year, they're more interested in sales than cases.

441
32:01.582 --> 32:04.562
I found one. So hang in there for a few more days.

442
32:04.562 --> 32:08.314
And ma'am, about losing that billboard spot...

443
32:08.314 --> 32:10.848
Just think of it as warding off bad luck.

444
32:10.848 --> 32:13.188
Once we expand to the eighth floor and grow,

445
32:13.188 --> 32:14.955
and once the new lawyer arrives,

446
32:14.955 --> 32:17.040
everything will go smoothly for us.

447
32:17.040 --> 32:19.440
It doesn't bother me.

448
32:19.440 --> 32:21.267
I'll focus on the eighth-floor expansion.

449
32:21.267 --> 32:22.667
Yes, ma'am.

450
32:25.230 --> 32:28.439
Ma'am, I'll head out first for my next trial.

451
32:28.439 --> 32:29.972
- Go on. - Thanks for the meal.

452
32:29.972 --> 32:32.247
- Good luck. - Yes, ma'am.

453
32:33.564 --> 32:35.495
Thank you for coming.

454
32:46.403 --> 32:48.480
Isn't that Park Tae Su from By the Law?

455
32:48.480 --> 32:49.572
It is.

456
32:49.572 --> 32:52.033
Aren't he and Cha Eun Kyung the top two in divorce?

457
32:52.033 --> 32:54.981
Judging by the view counts, he'll be number one soon.

458
32:54.981 --> 32:57.480
Already? How many views does he have?

459
32:57.480 --> 32:59.517
It's around 200,000.

460
32:59.517 --> 33:01.708
200,000?

461
33:04.189 --> 33:06.093
Park Tae Su.

462
33:07.412 --> 33:11.305
[Maximum Divorce Compensation] [People to Avoid]

463
33:11.305 --> 33:13.505
Is he even a lawyer?

464
33:13.505 --> 33:15.897
[Park Tae Su Answers Your Questions]

465
33:15.897 --> 33:18.669
What is the world coming to?

466
33:24.207 --> 33:25.233
Yes.

467
33:25.233 --> 33:27.215
Ma'am, we're in trouble.

468
33:27.215 --> 33:29.439
Someone else leased the eighth floor.

469
33:29.439 --> 33:32.023
What do you mean? We have a contract.

470
33:32.023 --> 33:34.969
They paid the penalty and offered double the rent for it.

471
33:34.969 --> 33:36.743
Double again?

472
33:37.731 --> 33:40.430
Who would do such a thing?

473
33:40.430 --> 33:42.317
Attorney Park Tae Su did.

474
33:47.522 --> 33:51.239
If you see Attorney Park Tae Su, let me know immediately.

475
33:51.239 --> 33:53.434
I need to see him right now.

476
33:58.385 --> 34:00.725
[Cool-headed Negotiations, Meticulous Lawsuits]

477
34:18.188 --> 34:19.787
Seaweed soup?

478
34:20.731 --> 34:23.053
You remember? It's your mom's birthday.

479
34:24.147 --> 34:28.672
Dad, did you forget who's responsible for us living like this?

480
34:29.439 --> 34:32.115
Haven't seen her in ages. She's not my mom.

481
34:33.605 --> 34:36.755
Still, she's your mother.

482
34:48.034 --> 34:51.600
No. She's not a mother. She's a perpetrator.

483
35:00.689 --> 35:02.298
Wrap that case up quickly.

484
35:02.298 --> 35:06.227
A divorce rookie like you can never beat Cha Eun Kyung.

485
35:06.227 --> 35:07.984
That's normal for a rookie.

486
35:07.984 --> 35:11.561
Try to broaden your perspective.

487
35:13.605 --> 35:16.005
I'm going to win this case.

488
35:31.276 --> 35:33.286
[5,000+ Cases: Cha's Argument Skills]

489
35:33.286 --> 35:35.731
5,000 cases?

490
35:35.731 --> 35:37.797
Is she that good?

491
35:39.188 --> 35:43.147
Today, we have Attorney Cha Eun Kyung. Hello, Attorney Cha.

492
35:43.147 --> 35:44.859
Hello.

493
35:44.859 --> 35:49.662
Attorney, I saw a case where a man lied about his mistress being his sister

494
35:49.662 --> 35:53.147
and lived with her and his wife in the same house.

495
35:53.147 --> 35:56.860
- That's insane. - Do people like that really exist?

496
35:56.860 --> 35:59.714
Reality always goes beyond any drama.

497
36:00.860 --> 36:03.480
What's with that nonchalant expression?

498
36:03.480 --> 36:07.748
Then do you have your own litigation tips?

499
36:07.748 --> 36:11.732
Minimize emotions and take the opponent's key keywords,

500
36:11.732 --> 36:14.736
then refute them head-on to highlight the core issues.

501
36:14.736 --> 36:18.272
For example, if the opponent claims "verbal abuse,"

502
36:18.272 --> 36:21.410
say, "It was an 'argument'" instead.

503
36:21.410 --> 36:25.457
Keywords are grounds for fault, so they stick in the judge's mind.

504
36:25.457 --> 36:27.442
Keyword refutation.

505
36:28.902 --> 36:30.856
[Keyword Refutation]

506
36:30.856 --> 36:33.047
- Yes, thank you. - Thank you.

507
36:39.355 --> 36:41.105
- Attorney, - Yes?

508
36:41.105 --> 36:44.412
Will this be enough to stop the divorce?

509
36:44.412 --> 36:46.939
Yes, this makes it worth a shot.

510
36:46.939 --> 36:48.064
Okay.

511
36:48.064 --> 36:49.348
- Let's go. - Okay.

512
36:55.647 --> 36:58.782
Thank you, Attorney. I'll be in touch.

513
36:58.782 --> 37:00.426
Thank you.

514
37:01.397 --> 37:03.672
- I'll show you out. - Sure.

515
37:10.480 --> 37:11.684
Yes.

516
37:13.064 --> 37:15.004
Ma'am, what should we do?

517
37:15.004 --> 37:19.551
Attorney Jeon's morning trial ran long, so he's not back in the office yet.

518
37:19.551 --> 37:21.316
Is that so?

519
37:21.316 --> 37:25.049
- Then I'll go to Park Na Yeon's trial. - Yes, ma'am.

520
37:33.205 --> 37:35.504
[TAESU Law Firm]

521
37:42.516 --> 37:46.828
The plaintiff told the defendant to go have sex with a new partner

522
37:46.828 --> 37:49.894
and constantly pressured her to have relations with others.

523
37:49.894 --> 37:55.252
His only reason was that their marriage needed a "refresh."

524
37:56.230 --> 37:59.797
That claim again? This is ridiculous.

525
38:01.564 --> 38:07.030
The defendant actually suggested group sex with three or four people.

526
38:07.030 --> 38:11.490
Evidence of the defendant recruiting group sex members has been submitted.

527
38:12.230 --> 38:13.856
Counsel for the defendant?

528
38:13.856 --> 38:17.047
Why don't we settle this and wrap it up here?

529
38:18.916 --> 38:20.614
We cannot settle.

530
38:20.614 --> 38:24.982
Your Honor, not all affairs are the same.

531
38:24.982 --> 38:28.204
Did a lawyer just make that claim?

532
38:28.930 --> 38:31.700
An affair is an affair.

533
38:31.700 --> 38:35.505
Are you claiming there are degrees of illegality in an affair?

534
38:36.397 --> 38:37.939
No.

535
38:37.939 --> 38:41.172
I'm claiming there is no illegality.

536
38:44.270 --> 38:48.342
If you're going to make such a ridiculous claim, provide some evidence.

537
38:50.605 --> 38:53.188
It's an open marriage agreement.

538
38:53.188 --> 38:56.318
What's this? Open marriage?

539
38:59.140 --> 39:01.415
[Open Marriage Agreement]

540
39:01.415 --> 39:03.304
An open marriage agreement,

541
39:03.304 --> 39:08.357
meaning a free sex or sexual freedom agreement.

542
39:16.894 --> 39:20.706
The plaintiff, Seo Ji Hoon, committed adultery "before" the agreement,

543
39:20.706 --> 39:24.690
while defendant Park Na Yeon only dated other men "after" it.

544
39:24.690 --> 39:27.105
Only the plaintiff is at fault.

545
39:27.105 --> 39:29.298
Please dismiss the divorce petition.

546
39:30.522 --> 39:33.077
Your Honor, the agreement never says

547
39:33.077 --> 39:38.284
the plaintiff threatened or coerced her to meet other men.

548
39:41.439 --> 39:44.522
Your Honor.

549
39:44.522 --> 39:49.755
I just "happened" to stray, but she cheated on purpose.

550
39:51.439 --> 39:52.720
It's okay.

551
39:52.720 --> 39:58.037
I mean, what man wouldn't fall for a woman's seduction?

552
40:00.059 --> 40:03.859
So, the plaintiff's infidelity was "accidental,"

553
40:03.859 --> 40:05.755
while hers was "intentional."

554
40:05.755 --> 40:07.225
Is that your argument?

555
40:07.225 --> 40:09.499
Yes, exactly.

556
40:10.188 --> 40:13.314
You have quite the legal mind.

557
40:13.314 --> 40:16.791
You hardly even need a lawyer.

558
40:32.361 --> 40:38.423
Interpreting "not interfering" as permission to date other people...

559
40:40.814 --> 40:44.047
is a subjective interpretation by defense counsel.

560
40:44.828 --> 40:49.317
The term "private life" is right there. How is that subjective?

561
40:49.317 --> 40:51.870
It's a standard interpretation.

562
40:51.870 --> 40:55.689
Minimize emotions and take the opponent's key keywords

563
40:55.689 --> 40:59.288
then refute them head-on to highlight the core issues.

564
40:59.986 --> 41:03.228
Are "private life" and "sex life" the same thing?

565
41:05.075 --> 41:07.698
Back in the game. Way to go, girl.

566
41:08.626 --> 41:10.802
I guess she's not a rookie.

567
41:12.359 --> 41:16.522
Private life or sex life, what does it matter?

568
41:16.522 --> 41:23.064
Courts have already ruled that infidelity doesn't require sex. Surely you know?

569
41:23.064 --> 41:28.381
That's not even the point. Let's focus on the actual issue.

570
41:38.513 --> 41:40.093
Why be like this?

571
41:40.093 --> 41:42.715
Why on earth would you lie to your own lawyer?

572
41:42.715 --> 41:44.564
An open marriage?

573
41:44.564 --> 41:49.911
Actually, it's my first marriage, but my wife's second.

574
41:49.911 --> 41:53.758
She said she tried it once and realized marriage wasn't for her.

575
41:53.758 --> 41:57.731
She said if she married again, she wanted to freely sleep with others.

576
41:57.731 --> 41:59.664
And I was okay with it.

577
41:59.664 --> 42:03.188
You might think I'm crazy, but at the time,

578
42:03.188 --> 42:06.273
I wanted to marry her so badly that I would do anything.

579
42:07.439 --> 42:10.299
I don't have proof,

580
42:10.299 --> 42:12.731
but my wife was definitely the first to cheat.

581
42:12.731 --> 42:14.468
So out of spite, I...

582
42:16.105 --> 42:18.937
But now she's pinning it all on me.

583
42:22.620 --> 42:23.850
See?

584
42:23.850 --> 42:27.480
You're not satisfied with just me either, are you?

585
42:27.480 --> 42:28.922
I'm sorry.

586
42:29.647 --> 42:34.410
I only did it because you kept seeing other men. I was just angry.

587
42:34.410 --> 42:36.992
It didn't mean anything.

588
42:36.992 --> 42:41.005
Manager Park from the pet shop kept hitting on me.

589
42:42.064 --> 42:43.689
No.

590
42:43.689 --> 42:45.397
Actually, this is better.

591
42:45.397 --> 42:51.188
Since it's come to this, let's just sign a formal agreement.

592
42:51.188 --> 42:53.314
- Here. - Honey, I'm sorry. Okay?

593
42:53.314 --> 42:54.605
I'll just...

594
42:54.605 --> 42:57.867
I have already signed it. You just need to sign here.

595
42:57.867 --> 42:59.809
Right here.

596
42:59.809 --> 43:01.514
Seo Ji Hoon.

597
43:20.188 --> 43:22.256
I need to take a call.

598
43:23.649 --> 43:24.907
Understood.

599
43:24.907 --> 43:29.156
I'm your attorney, so I'll trust you and defend you until the end.

600
43:30.188 --> 43:31.672
Thank you.

601
43:39.039 --> 43:44.379
The AL C&T wife you saw this morning signed with TAESU Law Firm.

602
43:44.976 --> 43:47.420
A case worth tens of billions of won...

603
43:47.420 --> 43:50.520
I can't believe she hired that attention-seeker.

604
43:56.355 --> 43:58.273
[Park Tae Su] But...

605
43:58.273 --> 44:01.814
Why is TAESU Law Firm's retainer so low?

606
44:01.814 --> 44:04.564
It's much cheaper than REBOM's.

607
44:04.564 --> 44:07.355
Instead, the success fee is double.

608
44:07.355 --> 44:11.594
We save clients' money where we can and make the other party pay.

609
44:11.594 --> 44:13.230
That's what real lawyers do.

610
44:13.230 --> 44:17.964
Then can I really get 50% of the assets?

611
44:20.001 --> 44:22.685
I don't set such limits.

612
44:22.685 --> 44:25.085
I'll get you as much as I can.

613
44:50.105 --> 44:53.522
I'm counting on you, Attorney Park.

614
45:09.105 --> 45:14.319
Wow, you were right. This is the best location.

615
45:14.319 --> 45:19.272
Most clients today said they stopped by after visiting REBOM.

616
45:19.272 --> 45:23.245
I told you. It's the perfect spot.

617
45:23.245 --> 45:26.939
Across from the court, above Cha Eun Kyung.

618
45:26.939 --> 45:31.522
If we charge half of REBOM's price, all their cases will come to us.

619
45:31.522 --> 45:35.314
Attorney Cha Eun Kyung called earlier.

620
45:35.314 --> 45:37.064
She wants to see you.

621
45:37.064 --> 45:38.287
Me?

622
45:40.023 --> 45:43.053
Tell her I'm out. Forever.

623
45:45.093 --> 45:48.314
[Consultation Lounge]

624
45:48.314 --> 45:53.467
Looking at today's trial, I think I was completely played.

625
45:53.467 --> 45:55.381
It was all a trap.

626
46:00.564 --> 46:04.064
- How could you do this to me? - Damn it, you're so annoying.

627
46:04.064 --> 46:07.439
How can someone be with only one person for their whole life?

628
46:07.439 --> 46:10.339
You don't excite me anymore.

629
46:11.741 --> 46:16.814
Since it's come to this, let's just enjoy ourselves.

630
46:16.814 --> 46:17.984
Okay?

631
46:17.984 --> 46:19.979
Life is short.

632
46:22.296 --> 46:26.714
Sign this and we stay together. If not, we get a divorce.

633
46:28.605 --> 46:30.423
Think carefully.

634
46:31.439 --> 46:33.731
Do you want to be a woman who divorced twice?

635
46:33.731 --> 46:35.922
Who would want you then?

636
46:49.355 --> 46:51.505
Good girl.

637
47:02.689 --> 47:05.772
[Married woman in 30s living in Seoul. Looking for a paid date]

638
47:05.772 --> 47:07.456
Show me.

639
47:10.519 --> 47:11.897
Keep going.

640
47:17.740 --> 47:19.974
- Same as before? - Ugh.

641
47:38.439 --> 47:39.963
So long.

642
47:41.812 --> 47:46.489
I signed that open marriage agreement because I didn't want a divorce.

643
47:46.489 --> 47:49.856
I even agreed to it to make this work...

644
47:49.856 --> 47:52.158
Even after being fooled,

645
47:52.158 --> 47:54.558
why can't I set for a divorce?

646
47:55.316 --> 47:57.897
A woman who divorced twice.

647
47:57.897 --> 48:00.505
You're afraid of that stigma.

648
48:04.171 --> 48:05.381
Yes.

649
48:06.397 --> 48:08.820
"A woman who divorced twice."

650
48:08.820 --> 48:11.090
I'm so scared of that title.

651
48:13.160 --> 48:17.672
Attorney, what are our chances of winning?

652
48:18.605 --> 48:20.918
As of now, it's fifty-fifty.

653
48:20.918 --> 48:22.572
Fifty-fifty?

654
48:23.336 --> 48:25.230
I thought...

655
48:25.230 --> 48:27.397
you were certain.

656
48:27.397 --> 48:29.297
I'm not certain.

657
48:29.939 --> 48:33.797
But a lawyer's job is to argue as if they are certain.

658
48:34.533 --> 48:39.621
No judge in the world rules for someone who lacks confidence in their own words.

659
48:46.627 --> 48:49.804
[CHUNJEONG: Fighting for clients with trust and responsibility]

660
48:49.804 --> 48:53.768
[All legal consultations are paid]

661
48:53.768 --> 48:55.968
[Corporate & Administrative Law] [Damages]

662
48:55.968 --> 48:58.494
Man, I'm exhausted.

663
48:59.307 --> 49:00.669
[Boss]

664
49:09.718 --> 49:13.295
♪ I promised to go to Seoul one day ♪

665
49:13.295 --> 49:16.454
♪ and become successful ♪

666
49:16.454 --> 49:20.223
♪ and come back ♪

667
49:20.223 --> 49:26.592
♪ But I got so busy crying and laughing ♪

668
49:26.592 --> 49:29.689
♪ that I can only go there in my dreams ♪

669
49:29.689 --> 49:32.671
Councilor, I thought Attorney Kang

670
49:32.671 --> 49:36.856
was only good at her job, but her singing is incredible too.

671
49:36.856 --> 49:38.939
Wow, Attorney Kang.

672
49:38.939 --> 49:44.588
They say people live up to their looks. You really do have talent.

673
49:46.675 --> 49:49.064
♪ My life is so lacking ♪

674
49:49.064 --> 49:54.266
♪ I write its diary ♪

675
49:54.266 --> 49:59.732
♪ while looking at the Seoul moon ♪

676
50:04.864 --> 50:08.264
I'm going to step out to the restroom.

677
50:08.981 --> 50:10.955
Sure, go ahead.

678
50:15.522 --> 50:18.480
It must have been urgent.

679
50:18.480 --> 50:22.065
- I'm counting on you, Partner Kim. - Don't you worry.

680
50:22.065 --> 50:24.638
I'll get back every cent you're owed.

681
50:24.638 --> 50:27.423
Don't worry. Who's the best at debt collection?

682
50:27.423 --> 50:28.656
Kang Hye Seong.

683
50:28.656 --> 50:31.105
- Kang Hye Seong. - Kang Hye Seong.

684
50:31.105 --> 50:32.429
It's a promise. A promise.

685
50:32.429 --> 50:35.064
- Promise. - Promise. Don't fail me.

686
50:35.064 --> 50:37.797
Please go in. Yes, go on in.

687
50:39.355 --> 50:41.964
- Get home safe. - I'm off.

688
50:45.188 --> 50:46.508
Sir,

689
50:47.713 --> 50:50.188
please stop making me go to these.

690
50:50.188 --> 50:54.461
And please take down that "Problem Solver" banner hanging downtown.

691
50:55.814 --> 51:00.230
You know that could break advertising rules under the Attorney-at-Law Act, right?

692
51:00.230 --> 51:01.670
Hey, Kang.

693
51:01.670 --> 51:05.064
Let go of trivial things! Or you'll never be number one in Gwangjin.

694
51:05.064 --> 51:08.140
Starting tomorrow, report to the city councilor's office.

695
51:09.856 --> 51:12.647
I have a case in Seoul tomorrow.

696
51:12.647 --> 51:16.689
You haven't finished that yet? I told you, it's not cost-effective!

697
51:16.689 --> 51:19.490
Are you telling me to just give up on the case?

698
51:19.490 --> 51:23.457
I told you to make concessions and settle. Didn't I tell you?

699
51:23.457 --> 51:25.675
You're not cut out for divorce cases.

700
51:25.675 --> 51:27.539
How many times have I told you?

701
51:28.750 --> 51:30.859
What's taking so long? Damn it.

702
51:40.474 --> 51:43.117
[Open Marriage Agreement]

703
51:51.564 --> 51:56.047
Divorce cases are a 1% fight, not a 99% one.

704
51:59.814 --> 52:02.000
Where are you going this late?

705
52:03.731 --> 52:05.588
To find that 1%.

706
52:23.191 --> 52:25.000
[My Daughter]

707
52:27.265 --> 52:28.272
Yeah?

708
52:28.272 --> 52:31.147
Can I stay at Dad's for two more days?

709
52:31.147 --> 52:32.316
Why all of a sudden?

710
52:32.316 --> 52:35.046
I just want to spend more time with Ji Yoon.

711
52:37.207 --> 52:39.675
Visitation is an agreement too,

712
52:39.675 --> 52:42.347
so how about we plan the extra night in advance?

713
52:42.347 --> 52:44.413
We promised to do homework together.

714
52:45.147 --> 52:46.772
Okay.

715
52:46.772 --> 52:48.685
- Don't stay up too... - Thanks, Mom.

716
52:48.685 --> 52:50.230
Hello?

717
52:50.230 --> 52:52.746
- What did she say? - She said yes.

718
52:56.272 --> 52:58.468
Oh, boy.

719
53:03.471 --> 53:05.437
[Central Family Court]

720
53:10.183 --> 53:13.715
The defendant still doesn't want a divorce.

721
53:16.272 --> 53:17.672
However.

722
53:18.272 --> 53:20.260
What? No way.

723
53:20.260 --> 53:22.981
If the terms we have brought are accepted,

724
53:22.981 --> 53:27.423
she is willing to agree to a divorce and settle right here.

725
53:30.230 --> 53:34.089
Did she persuade someone who didn't want a divorce?

726
53:39.212 --> 53:40.404
I...

727
53:41.196 --> 53:44.014
I really don't want a divorce.

728
53:44.014 --> 53:46.232
Please. You must win this case.

729
53:47.480 --> 53:53.089
But if you win the case, will you really win at life as well, Park Na Yeon?

730
53:54.064 --> 53:57.367
You won't become a woman who divorced twice,

731
53:57.367 --> 54:02.172
but is the plaintiff a partner worth keeping this much?

732
54:03.267 --> 54:04.662
Is he?

733
54:25.689 --> 54:31.230
The condition is that we take 100% of the condo, which is your joint property.

734
54:31.230 --> 54:35.272
We can't accept that. That condo was gifted by Seo Ji Hoon's father.

735
54:35.272 --> 54:39.011
Then let's make it 70-30. 70 for us, 30 for you.

736
54:39.011 --> 54:40.677
Absolutely not.

737
54:40.677 --> 54:44.306
It's separate property. The marriage lasted under ten years with no kids.

738
54:44.306 --> 54:46.101
70-30 is ridiculous.

739
54:49.105 --> 54:51.755
I said I'm fine with it.

740
55:03.188 --> 55:06.172
I'll accept the mediation proposal.

741
55:13.373 --> 55:17.130
These are market price reports for the condo from ten realtors.

742
55:18.470 --> 55:23.064
The average price is 130 million won. 70% of that is 91 million won.

743
55:23.064 --> 55:27.731
So, you just need to pay us 40 million won in cash.

744
55:27.731 --> 55:31.672
She's inflating the market value to get a bigger payout.

745
55:32.531 --> 55:35.247
Did she really go and get all those herself?

746
55:41.105 --> 55:44.023
It's not 130 million won. It's 100 million won.

747
55:44.023 --> 55:48.297
Seems you didn't check the Ministry of Land price data or bank AI valuation.

748
55:51.105 --> 55:53.096
Oh, no.

749
55:53.718 --> 55:55.013
Wait.

750
56:02.897 --> 56:05.721
That area is scheduled for reconstruction.

751
56:05.721 --> 56:08.623
The market price is clearly going to rise.

752
56:08.623 --> 56:11.321
A clear rise in the market price?

753
56:11.321 --> 56:15.147
Exactly. So 130 million won sounds good, right?

754
56:15.147 --> 56:18.051
If you're so sure, how about this?

755
56:18.051 --> 56:22.094
Take the title of the condo and give us 90 million won,

756
56:22.094 --> 56:24.731
which is 70% of 130 million won.

757
56:24.731 --> 56:26.131
What?

758
56:27.230 --> 56:32.350
No, we don't have that much cash right now...

759
56:32.350 --> 56:35.625
I did my best to score an own goal.

760
56:36.230 --> 56:40.639
Unfortunately, if we can't agree on the market price,

761
56:40.639 --> 56:43.564
we'll just scrap today's mediation.

762
56:43.564 --> 56:45.397
We'll withdraw consent to divorce.

763
56:45.397 --> 56:49.339
You're so annoyingly clingy.

764
56:50.064 --> 56:52.964
Hey, take it all.

765
56:53.602 --> 56:55.090
Just give it to her, okay?

766
56:55.090 --> 56:57.454
- You're unbelievable... - What?

767
57:31.315 --> 57:34.094
Seo Ji Hoon, were you always like this?

768
57:34.094 --> 57:36.210
Why did you step in like that?

769
57:36.210 --> 57:39.311
You were tricked by the lawyer Cha. You lost the condo!

770
57:39.311 --> 57:42.230
Forget it. It's not even worth that much.

771
57:42.230 --> 57:45.215
I'll call it buying my freedom with pocket change.

772
57:47.147 --> 57:50.278
It feels so good to finally get rid of that clingy woman.

773
57:54.807 --> 57:57.316
Since you revealed your true colors, let me ask.

774
57:57.316 --> 57:59.307
That agreement,

775
57:59.307 --> 58:03.314
did you threaten your spouse into signing it to justify your own cheating?

776
58:03.314 --> 58:05.547
Why did you go that far?

777
58:06.230 --> 58:11.256
How can you only love one person? That's neglecting my duties.

778
58:13.439 --> 58:18.397
Good things only have value when they are shared with everyone.

779
58:18.397 --> 58:21.578
Free sex is beneficial to humanity.

780
58:21.578 --> 58:24.574
You should try being generous too.

781
58:26.111 --> 58:28.814
Thanks for your hard work.

782
58:28.814 --> 58:31.547
Hey babe. Yeah, it's all over.

783
58:39.614 --> 58:43.314
Thank you, Attorney Cha.

784
58:43.314 --> 58:48.522
I almost spent my life with that man because I cared too much about what others think.

785
58:48.522 --> 58:51.052
I was just doing my job.

786
58:51.052 --> 58:55.314
I hope the reconstruction happens, just as Attorney Kang said.

787
58:55.314 --> 58:58.672
When you live alone, a house is your best partner.

788
58:59.897 --> 59:01.597
Well, then.

789
59:22.897 --> 59:24.317
Attorney Cha!

790
59:28.064 --> 59:29.325
Attorney.

791
59:30.981 --> 59:33.540
You did a great job, Attorney Cha.

792
59:33.540 --> 59:37.397
Now she's all smiles since the case is over.

793
59:37.397 --> 59:39.522
You did a great job too, Attorney Kang.

794
59:39.522 --> 59:43.630
And I'm not a newbie. I'm in my fifth year.

795
59:44.814 --> 59:46.173
Fifth year.

796
59:47.101 --> 59:48.774
Yes, well.

797
59:55.856 --> 59:57.897
Attorney Kang?

798
59:57.897 --> 59:59.475
Yes?

799
59:59.475 --> 01:00:03.449
Park Na Yeon. She really didn't sleep with anyone.

800
01:00:03.449 --> 01:00:05.306
You may not believe me, but...

801
01:00:06.497 --> 01:00:08.218
I believe you.

802
01:00:08.218 --> 01:00:10.397
So you knew?

803
01:00:10.397 --> 01:00:12.106
Whether we knew or not,

804
01:00:12.106 --> 01:00:15.597
we have to do our best to fight for our clients.

805
01:00:15.597 --> 01:00:18.149
That's our job. Is it not, Attorney Cha?

806
01:00:21.439 --> 01:00:22.612
That's right.

807
01:00:23.312 --> 01:00:25.292
Thank you for your hard work.

808
01:00:25.939 --> 01:00:27.362
You as well.

809
01:01:00.981 --> 01:01:06.547
Ma'am, the lawyer you hired won't be able to join us.

810
01:01:15.025 --> 01:01:17.615
Are "private life" and "sex life" the same thing?

811
01:01:17.615 --> 01:01:19.493
Your Honor, the agreement never says

812
01:01:19.493 --> 01:01:24.772
the plaintiff threatened or coerced her to meet other men.

813
01:01:24.772 --> 01:01:27.939
These are market price reports for the condo from ten realtors.

814
01:01:27.939 --> 01:01:31.221
It was obvious her client stabbed her in the back,

815
01:01:31.221 --> 01:01:33.848
but she kept cool so the judge wouldn't notice.

816
01:01:33.848 --> 01:01:35.064
Understood.

817
01:01:35.064 --> 01:01:38.564
I'm your attorney, so I'll trust you and defend you until the end.

818
01:01:38.564 --> 01:01:41.925
We have to do our best to fight for our clients.

819
01:01:41.925 --> 01:01:46.534
She did her best for her client and fought until the end.

820
01:01:48.689 --> 01:01:51.147
I'm not a newbie. I'm in my fifth year.

821
01:01:51.147 --> 01:01:54.482
At least five years' experience, serious about divorce,

822
01:01:54.482 --> 01:01:56.248
and good at handling cases.

823
01:01:56.248 --> 01:01:58.630
She's perfect for divorce cases.

824
01:02:00.744 --> 01:02:02.407
Found you.

825
01:02:10.925 --> 01:02:11.939
Yes.

826
01:02:11.939 --> 01:02:15.808
Ma'am. I heard Attorney Park Tae Su is in his office right now.

827
01:02:15.808 --> 01:02:17.208
Okay.

828
01:02:18.397 --> 01:02:20.956
Mr. Kim, please head back to the office.

829
01:02:20.956 --> 01:02:22.570
Yes, ma'am.

830
01:02:35.607 --> 01:02:36.897
[TAESU Law Firm]

831
01:03:24.911 --> 01:03:26.264
[Park Tae Su]

832
01:03:46.439 --> 01:03:49.005
Do you have anything else to say?

833
01:03:58.564 --> 01:04:00.660
Attorney Park Tae Su.

834
01:04:13.689 --> 01:04:15.263
Eun Kyung?

835
01:04:18.158 --> 01:04:19.428
Eun Kyung.

836
01:05:35.772 --> 01:05:39.897
You signed with another firm. TAESU Law Firm?

837
01:05:39.897 --> 01:05:41.772
Good morning, Attorney Cha.

838
01:05:41.772 --> 01:05:43.736
Do you know Attorney Park?

839
01:05:43.736 --> 01:05:46.743
We went to college together. He's such a copycat.

840
01:05:46.743 --> 01:05:47.981
So you remembered.

841
01:05:47.981 --> 01:05:50.023
I think I found one.

842
01:05:50.023 --> 01:05:53.898
Then how about making TAESU your next step?

843
01:05:53.898 --> 01:05:58.133
Attorney Park, can we meet tomorrow?
